  "root_cause": {
    "writer_non_atomic": "automation/state/fleet/build_shared_signal.py -- every sig-emitting branch in build() ends with OUT.write_text(json.dumps(sig, indent=2), encoding=\"utf-8\") (lines ~720,744,835; build_from_rows has its own guarded copies at ~1333,1392) -- Path.write_text opens in \"w\" mode which TRUNCATES the file to 0 bytes before writing the new content, and is not an atomic replace.",
    "reader_no_retry": "automation/state/fleet/fleet_live.py:112-119 _load_signal() does path.read_text() + json.loads() ONCE, no retry, no lock; on JSONDecodeError/OSError returns (None, f\"signal_unreadable: {e}\").",
    "two_independent_writers": {
      "writer_1": "Gamma_FleetExecutor (every 1 min, 09:31-16:01 ET) -- step 1 of setup/scripts/run-fleet-executor.ps1 calls build_shared_signal.py as its own process, THEN (serially, same script) step 2 calls fleet_live.py to read. No race within one fleet-executor invocation; -MultipleInstances IgnoreNew (setup/install-fleet-executor.ps1) prevents overlap with itself.",
      "writer_2": "Gamma_SightBeacon (every 1 min, 09:00-16:30 ET) -- INDEPENDENT scheduled task. setup/scripts/sight_beacon.py main() calls build_shared_signal.build() unconditionally every fire (\"Drive the fleet's shared-signal off this beacon every minute\" -- sight_beacon.py:185-193), targeting the SAME automation/state/fleet/shared-signal.json. This second writer is NOT phase-locked to Gamma_FleetExecutor -- two independently-scheduled Windows Tasks with no shared mutex."
